       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little extra blood pressure control.\n\nYou have a few options:\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Enter 5 mg PO once daily**, if the patient is starting therapy. The usual start is 2.5\u20135 mg.\n3. **Enter 20 mg PO once daily as written**, if the dose is intentional. If so, please confirm and I'll add a note such as \"Dose above labeled maximum, confirmed by attending.\"\n\nIf blood pressure isn't controlled on 10 mg, adding a second agent is usually preferred. A typical choice is an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-like diuretic.\n\nWhich option do you want?"
      }
     ],
